claim.claim-text:
a base substrate (1000, 2000), comprising a display region (1100) and a bonding region (1200, 2200) located at least one side of the display region (1100);
a plurality of sub-pixels (110, 210), located in the display region (1100);
a plurality of data lines (1101), located in the display region (1100) and configured to provide data signals to the plurality of sub-pixels (110, 210);
a plurality of data leads (1220, 2220), located in the bonding region (1200, 2200) and electrically connected with the plurality of data lines (1101);
at least one group of contact pads, located in the bonding region (1200, 2200), wherein the at least one group of contact pads comprise a plurality of contact pads (1210, 2210), at least one of the plurality of contact pads (1210, 2210) comprises a first contact pad metal layer (1215, 2215) and a second contact pad metal layer (1217, 2217), the first contact pad metal layer (1215, 2215) is located on a side of the plurality of data leads (1220, 2220) away from the base substrate (1000, 2000) and is electrically connected with one of the plurality of data leads (1220, 2220), the second contact pad metal layer (1217, 2217) is located on a side of the first contact pad metal layer (1215, 2215) away from the base substrate (1000, 2000) and is electrically connected with the first contact pad metal layer (1215, 2215), and the second contact pad metal layer (1217, 2217) covers an edge of the first contact pad metal layer (1215, 2215);
a first insulation layer (1230, 2230), located in the bonding region (1200, 2200), wherein the first insulation layer (1230, 2230) is located in gaps between the plurality of contact pads (1210, 2210) and covers edges of the plurality of contact pads (1210, 2210), and exposes surfaces of the plurality of contact pads (1210, 2210) facing away from the base substrate (1000, 2000); and
at least one bonding region insulation layer, located in the bonding region (1200, 2200), and a portion of the at least one bonding region insulation layer is located between the first contact pad metal layer (1215, 2215) and the data leads (1220, 2220), wherein the at least one bonding region insulation layer continuously extends from a position between the first contact pad metal layer (1215, 2215) and the data leads (1220, 2220) to a position between the first insulation layer (1230, 2230) and the base substrate (1000, 2000).

a pixel drive circuit (1120, 2120), comprising a thin film transistor, the thin film transistor comprises a gate electrode (11211, 21211), a source electrode (1125, 2125) and a drain electrode (1126, 2126), the source electrode (1125, 2125) and the drain electrode (1126, 2126) are located in a first display region metal layer (1127, 2127) at a side of the gate electrode (11211, 21211) away from the base substrate (1000, 2000), wherein the first display region metal layer (1127, 2127) and the first contact pad metal layer (1215, 2215) are provided at a same layer;
a first transfer electrode (1180, 2180), located at a side of the first display region metal layer (1127, 2127) away from the base substrate (1000, 2000), and electrically connected to the pixel drive circuit (1120, 2120), wherein the first transfer electrode (1180, 2180) and the second contact pad metal layer (1217, 2217) are provided at a same layer; and
a light emitting element (1140, 2140), electrically connected to the first transfer electrode (1180, 2180).
